+# Issue 26 — maintainer engine acceptance
+
+Status: **NOT RUN**. Complete after a full game restart with the normal **hhhh** playset. The changes are already installed in its regular local mod. Use a new 1776 game for initialization tests; an old save is useful only as a separate regression test. Record the executable version/build and active DLCs.
+
+1. **Load and initialize.** Start a new game on 1 January 1776. Confirm the date and normal first-day progress. Capture initial support and its tooltip for the American Revolution. Expected range: **0–100**; initial support need not always be 100. Native initialization has floors of 50, or 75 for negotiators. Check loading logs for malformed/unknown defines or unresolved macro values, especially `zz_1776_scenario.txt`.
+2. **Observe a changing war.** Advance the American conflict through battles, losses, occupation and time. Compare the support tooltip with those events. Native drift targets 50, but other factors can outweigh drift; this is not a promise of monotonic movement. Values must remain in 0–100. Below 25, check native low-support consequences. Record whether zero support causes an unexpected old-style automatic surrender. Follow the conflict through peace where practicable; record any war-goal scripting failures separately under #32.
+3. **Test an ordinary second conflict.** Use a separate normal interstate war, not a revolution, secession or uprising. Observe the same range and changing factors, then peace/enforcement. If both war leaders meet the native zero-support stalemate conditions, verify the six-month stalemate rule. Record dates and tooltips; do not treat a special-war exception as a failed ordinary-war test. If the conditions never occur, mark this subtest **not exercised**, not passed.
+4. **Save and reload.** Save during a running war, reload it and advance again. Verify support persistence and continued updates. Where feasible also reload after peace and check that the concluded war stays concluded. Compare new parser/runtime errors with the #20 baseline, including rotated logs; preserve the save and logs for any failure.
+5. **Check the label requested during delivery.** In France's journal, inspect the expansion group heading: **Guerres napoléoniennes** (English: **Napoleonic Wars**). Its natural-borders entry must still be **Les frontières naturelles de la France**. If the entry/group is not currently available, record that the visual check was not exercised; this localization change does not alter activation conditions.
+
+The retained base working-adult ratio is 0.30 and all pre-existing demographic formulas are statically identical. Population-specific effective employment ratios can include laws and other modifiers; do not require every displayed ratio to equal the base value. Verify that a fresh game retains plausible scenario initialization and no demographic macro-loading errors.
+
+Evidence to attach: game version/DLCs, country and start date, support tooltips before and after changes (including low support if reached), peace/stalemate dates and eligibility, save/reload result, journal heading screenshot when available, save name and relevant new log errors. Mark each item **passed**, **failed** or **not exercised**. Only the maintainer can supply human acceptance; no unchecked item is implicitly passed.
