+# Issue #27 - Sick Man of Europe continuation and direct local installation
+
+Date: 2026-11-07. Parent workstream #24; coordination #19; baseline #20; PR #34.
+Status: **IMPLEMENTED_READY_FOR_RUNTIME_VALIDATION**. Static checks pass; no in-game acceptance is claimed.
+
+## Delivery and preserved work
+
+The maintainer explicitly requested direct installation into the regular local mod used by the existing
+playset, rather than requiring manual retrieval or a separate demo copy. The active launcher database was
+read in **read-only mode**: playset **hhhh** is active and contains one enabled mod, pointing to the regular
+`1776_Age_of_Revolutions_fork` working directory. No launcher database edit was made.
+
+The previous six-file journal batch is now installed there. The two previously authorized native copper-icon
+references were also installed; the accepted naval AI category correction already matched and was preserved.
+The initial catch-up verified every destination against either its existing corrected contents or the clean
+recorded Git base before writing. It wrote 14 files and retained every pre-existing Git status entry.
+Original source bytes were backed up outside the mod. No checkout, reset, main merge, historical map change,
+law-audit change, resource redistribution or extra registered mod/playset was created.
+
+The new gameplay scope is **one file only**: `common/journal_entries/00_sick_man.txt`, based on remote
+`hotfix/1.15` parent `1b9416263775c56e607c86af9fbbe490feef7077`. The local source matched that parent before
+the bounded migration. The reusable read-only journal audit is extended with an explicit `--batch sick-man`
+option; its existing `first` default remains supported.
+
+## Contract and compatibility choices
+
+The canonical installed 1.15 `common/journal_entries/journal_entries.md:134-197` documents conclusion
+`outcome` blocks, owning-country root scopes, required descriptions, and `hidden invalid_outcome` flags.
+It explicitly requires **no trigger** on a timeout outcome and at most one such outcome. Current vanilla
+`00_sick_man.txt:14-105` supplies the completion/timeout example. Its timeout presentation uses
+`JOURNAL_ENTRY_TIMEOUT`, `JOURNAL_ENTRY_ON_TIMEOUT` and `JOURNAL_ENTRY_TIMEOUT_CONCLUSION_DESC`.
+These three keys and the six standard completion/failure keys were verified in unmasked English and French
+base-game localization files. No new player-facing prose is introduced.
+
+This migration retains the **mod's** authored criteria, rather than importing unrelated vanilla revisions:
+
+- The main journal still needs **four reform points** and retains its exact **10,950-day** timeout.
+- Syria/Egypt retain the original ownership and subject checks; the new vanilla uncontested-ownership and
+  subject-release conditions are not substituted.
+- Economy, education, army and bureaucracy thresholds, technologies, laws and scopes remain unchanged.
+- Separatism retains its strict `< 0.5` success/accumulation and `> 0.5` failure conditions, monthly pulse,
+  180-point goal, event lists and DLC-dependent Eastern Crisis path.
+- All eight success effects, the separatism failure effect and the main timeout effect retain every token
+  and effect order, including modifiers, claims, delayed/triggered events, variables and culture scopes.
+- The three Rumelian tradition removals in the timeout branch are retained, as is conditional removal of
+  `outmoded_bureaucracy` in the bureaucracy success branch.
+- Seven silent invalidations still test the original `sick_man_complete` condition; their original absent
+  handlers remain empty effects. No new cleanup effect or historical/subgoal flag is invented.
+- Modifiers while active, immediate/weekly/monthly behavior, progress bars, transfer/inheritance flags,
+  weights, pinning and the relative declaration order of authored conclusion predicates are preserved.
+
+The old and new engines' behavior when multiple predicates become true together, or at the exact timeout
+boundary, has not been measured in-game. Preserving source order and predicate tokens does not certify that
+engine-level precedence. Automatic removal of active modifiers and forced external journal removal also need
+runtime checks. In particular, vanilla cleanup helpers absent from the mod's original handlers are not copied
+blindly into the effects.
+
+## Explicit mapping
+
+All lines below refer to `common/journal_entries/00_sick_man.txt`.
+
+| Journal | Original definition line | New outcome lines | Mapping |
+| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
+| `je_sick_man_main` | 1 | 10, 27 | Completion; timeout with original effect, no trigger. |
+| `je_sick_man_syria` | 96 | 113, 175 | Completion; silent invalidation. |
+| `je_sick_man_egypt` | 184 | 212, 241 | Completion; silent invalidation. |
+| `je_sick_man_economy` | 229 | 268, 290 | Completion; silent invalidation. |
+| `je_sick_man_education` | 267 | 317, 341 | Completion; silent invalidation. |
+| `je_sick_man_separatism` | 318 | 379, 399, 421 | Completion; failure; silent invalidation. |
+| `je_sick_man_army` | 401 | 479, 518 | Completion; silent invalidation. |
+| `je_sick_man_bureaucracy` | 464 | 553, 580 | Completion; silent invalidation. |
+
+## Verification on the installed local files
+
+```text
+python tools/compatibility/issue27_journal_outcomes_audit.py --batch sick-man --mod-root MOD --baseline-root BEFORE --vanilla-root "C:/Games/Victoria 3/game" --inventory-root MOD
